// Title: Suspicious History File Operations
// Sigma ID: 508a9374-ad52-4789-b568-fc358def2c65
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Mikhail Larin, oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-17 | Modified: 2021-11-27
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1552.003
// Description: Detects commandline operations on shell history files
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrative activity
//   - Legitimate software, cleaning hist file
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1552.003/T1552.003.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_susp_histfile_operations.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains ".bash_history" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".zsh_history" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".zhistory" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".history" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".sh_history" or ProcessCommandLine contains "fish_history"
